{
  "tile": 32,
  "span": 4,
  "heightStep": 16,
  "storey": 64,
  "projection": "2:1 isometric at the terrain's texel density: screen x = U - V, screen y = (U + V) / 2 - Z, in texels (U = world X, V = world Z, Z = height); a 32 px tile is a 64x32 diamond, a 16 px height step 16 px of screen. Light from the top-left: tops 1.0, +Z faces 0.80, +X faces 0.62",
  "sampling": {
    "wall": "128x64, one storey per period. U = world distance along the face / (span * tile), measured left to right as the face is seen (along +X on +Z faces, along -Z on +X faces); V = height above the storey's floor / storey (repeats). Posts of timber_frame fall on tile edges",
    "roof": "128x128. On a slope: U = distance along the ridge / (span * tile), V = distance down the slope from the ridge / (span * tile): courses run along U, lower edges down V. As a flat top: UV = world XZ / (span * tile)",
    "floor": "128x128 tops: UV = world XZ / (span * tile), as terrain tops",
    "decal/wall": "alpha, authored face-on: 32 px (one tile) wide, bottom row = the storey's floor (doors and windows land at the right height on any storey); rose_window, crack and notices are 32x32 and go anywhere on a face. Placed in face space, never mirrored",
    "decal/floor": "alpha, tile-local on tops: rug is 64x64 across 2x2 tiles (from its back corner tile), doormat 32x32"
  },
